---
// Company. Short by design: one line, the founder quote, the founder note, one call to action.
// Copy is owner-supplied, verbatim. No biography, credentials, photo, or hospitality/culinary references.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Company — EdTerm"
  description="EdTerm is a healthcare data infrastructure company building the reasoning layer."
>
  <Hero label="Company" headline="EdTerm is a healthcare data infrastructure company building the reasoning layer." />

  <Section tone="white" layout="stack" id="founder">
    <figure>
      <blockquote class="font-quote text-quote italic text-navy">
        <p>“You can read something in a book, or you can do it for 30 years. They are not the same.”</p>
      </blockquote>
    </figure>

    <div class="space-y-4 pt-10 sm:pt-14">
      <p>
        The most useful knowledge was never in the classroom. I knew that early. It lives in people: in what they’ve
        learned from doing the work, and the judgment no manual can hand over.
      </p>
      <p>
        For two decades I’ve followed that question around the world, from Nepal to Alaska to the Mariana Islands,
        studying how apprenticeships, institutions and civilizations pass wisdom from one person to the next, and where
        that passing breaks.
      </p>
      <p>
        EdTerm is built for the place it breaks: capturing expert reasoning before it’s lost, and putting it where
        others can use it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="pt-6 font-display font-bold text-purple-700">Cameron Covarrubias, Founder</p>
  </Section>

  <CTA heading="Early Access" buttonLabel="Start a conversation" />
</BaseLayout>
